We investigate the impact of modified gravity on galaxy clustering and intrinsic alignments (IA) within the context of the Horndeski scalar-tensor theory. Our analysis focuses on the specific case where the Horndeski function $G_4$ depends on the scalar field $\phi$ and the combination of the Ricci scalar $R$ and the kinetic term $X$, defined as $X = - rac{1}{2}
