u}\phi$. By examining the behavior of the scalar field, we demonstrate that the model mimics a scale-invariant modification to gravity. Consequently, the scale-dependent terms in the linear matter power spectrum and the two-point IA function are altered. We quantify these effects by calculating the scale-dependent bias and the IA function under the influence of the modified Horndeski model, comparing our results against predictions from General Relativity. Our findings indicate that the scale-dependent bias and IA function are sensitive to the magnitude of the modified Horndeski parameter, $\alpha$. Furthermore, we analyze the scale-dependence of the IA function and find that it exhibits a significant scale-dependent component, which is notably larger than that of the galaxy clustering bias.
